1
00:00:02,420 --> 00:00:05,040
She is, in short,
the incarnation of the sea.

2
00:00:05,340 --> 00:00:09,340
Surfing, sailing, fishing,
jet skiing, scuba diving...

3
00:00:09,340 --> 00:00:12,720
Whatever you'd call a "marine sport,"
she's a natural at it.

4
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:15,180
Any competition she enters, she wins.

5
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,760
No one else even comes close.

6
00:00:17,470 --> 00:00:19,520
And her knowledge is just as impressive.

7
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:22,060
From nautical expertise to oceanography...

8
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:24,940
she can go toe-to-toe
with professionals in any field.

9
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:26,730
As someone once joked...

10
00:00:26,730 --> 00:00:30,320
"The only thing she's missing is gills."

11
00:00:32,570 --> 00:00:33,860
A Unicorn.

12
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:35,660
The Mermaid Queen...

13
00:00:37,780 --> 00:00:39,540
Mai Otohime!

14
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:44,040
Hey. Nice to meet ya.

15
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:19,930
It wasn't exactly a coincidence that 
I wound up judging the ramen contest.

16
00:02:19,930 --> 00:02:21,640
I came here for a reason,

17
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:24,100
but my other self was standing around
all fidgety in the hall,

18
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:26,020
and someone called out to her.

19
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:29,900
Though when you tried to make me
eat Noren Mitsuoka's nightmare ramen...

20
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:32,480
I thought I was gonna die
before I even got to make my entrance.

21
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:34,690
Wh-What is with this girl?

22
00:02:34,690 --> 00:02:36,360
What reason?

23
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:39,530
A Unicorn here to talk to Ogami?
Which means...

24
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:42,830
C'mon, after everything that's happened
so far, you've figured it out, right?

25
00:02:44,370 --> 00:02:45,830
A Mitsuoka duel!

26
00:02:45,830 --> 00:02:47,830
Let's throw down, you and I, Juzo!

27
00:02:47,830 --> 00:02:50,460
What? Wait, no, more like, we knew it!

28
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:51,710
Huh?

29
00:02:51,710 --> 00:02:52,340
HUH...?

30
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:53,840
Hold on, how would that even work?

31
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:58,300
A Mitsuoka duel is basically a fight
to decide Noren's boyfriend, right?

32
00:02:58,300 --> 00:03:01,140
If a girl challenges him... Wait. Can she?

33
00:03:01,510 --> 00:03:02,640
She can.

34
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:07,480
I read through the guidelines, and nowhere
does prohibit women from dueling.

35
00:03:07,480 --> 00:03:09,770
It just says the person who dates her
has to be male.

36
00:03:10,270 --> 00:03:13,440
If Juzo wins, he keeps his right
to be her boyfriend.

37
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:17,940
If I win, Juzo loses that right,
but I don't gain it, either.

38
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:19,780
Meaning the position becomes vacant.

39
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:24,990
And if that happens, other people
can duel to fill the vacancy.

40
00:03:24,990 --> 00:03:28,200
It's like when there's a title up 
for grabs in boxing or whatever.

41
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:29,330
Huh?

42
00:03:29,330 --> 00:03:33,210
Then there's no benefit for you, Otohime!
What are you even doing this for?

43
00:03:33,670 --> 00:03:37,210
Bingo! Honestly, the duel thing
was just my way into the conversation.

44
00:03:37,210 --> 00:03:38,800
I don't really care either way.

45
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:42,010
Even I get nervous
jumping straight to the point, y'know.

46
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:46,890
When I saw that futsal match against Tenma
Tendo, something hit me like lightning!

47
00:03:46,890 --> 00:03:50,310
Everyone's handwaving it away because of
the news about Tenma getting hurt...

48
00:03:50,310 --> 00:03:51,730
but you can't fool me.

49
00:03:52,060 --> 00:03:52,980
Juzo...

50
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:54,860
You're actually incredible, aren't you?

51
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:57,940
And then the other day,
you saved me from that accident, right?

52
00:03:57,940 --> 00:04:01,280
That's when my other self
felt the same way, too!

53
00:04:01,650 --> 00:04:04,660
Like, completely!
One hundred percent in love!

54
00:04:05,530 --> 00:04:06,990
I like you, Juzo!

55
00:04:06,990 --> 00:04:08,790
Go out with me!

56
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:10,790
What?

57
00:04:11,330 --> 00:04:12,790
What?

58
00:04:13,460 --> 00:04:14,290
Huh?

59
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:17,800
More trouble...

60
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:20,170
Wait... Huh?

61
00:04:20,170 --> 00:04:21,800
I mean, even if he's not into me,

62
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:24,760
any guy should be short-circuiting
at least a little right now, right?

63
00:04:24,760 --> 00:04:27,810
But he's not excited at all!
He's wilting! Is this guy for real?

64
00:04:28,220 --> 00:04:29,560
Okay...

65
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:32,440
Let me make sure
I've got this straight.

66
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:36,020
You want to beat me in a duel
so that Mitsuoka and I will break up,

67
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:38,650
and then date me once I'm single.
Is that right?

68
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:43,030
Even if I were single,
I wouldn't go out with you.

69
00:04:43,030 --> 00:04:44,700
The truth is, there are...

70
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:47,490
a lot of circumstances around
why I'm dating Mitsuoka right now.

71
00:04:47,490 --> 00:04:50,240
But I'm not actually planning
to date anyone.

72
00:04:51,330 --> 00:04:52,370
I'm sorry.

73
00:05:00,460 --> 00:05:03,800
Nice! That coolheaded side
of you is nice, too!

74
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:06,930
And I love how you instantly grasped the 
situation and give me a clean answer!

75
00:05:06,930 --> 00:05:09,470
Like I said, the duel part
doesn't really matter!

76
00:05:09,970 --> 00:05:11,140
I'm not giving up!

77
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:13,980
I'll keep coming at you as many times
as it takes until you like me!

78
00:05:14,350 --> 00:05:15,190
Wha...

79
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:17,110
Wait a second!

80
00:05:17,110 --> 00:05:18,860
What do you mean,
"The duel doesn't matter"?

81
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:21,820
Technically, he and 
I are dating right now!

82
00:05:21,820 --> 00:05:25,030
Huh? I'm only trying to make you
break up through a duel...

83
00:05:25,030 --> 00:05:28,240
because I thought that'd
 be a little more civilized.

84
00:05:28,740 --> 00:05:32,750
But really, why should I care whether 
the guy I like has a girlfriend?

85
00:05:32,750 --> 00:05:34,500
Either way, I'm gonna make my move.

86
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:36,670
And I'm confident
I can make him fall for me.

87
00:05:36,670 --> 00:05:40,710
All it comes down to is choosing whoever
seems better. Whoever seems superior.

88
00:05:40,710 --> 00:05:43,260
Male or female, that's how animals work.

89
00:05:43,550 --> 00:05:45,590
Oh, so that's the kind of girl she is.

90
00:05:45,590 --> 00:05:47,260
A carnivore woman!

91
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:52,100
Besides, Juzo just said
he doesn't actually plan on dating anyone.

92
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:54,180
So, it's not like you two
are in love, right?

93
00:05:54,180 --> 00:05:56,600
That makes this even more 
my business and mine alone.

94
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:59,060
Maybe I was a little too honest.

95
00:06:00,190 --> 00:06:02,400
You've got a lot of nerve,
talking like that!

96
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:04,820
It is not just your business, dumbass!

97
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:09,280
- Then duel me, Mai Otohime!
- Huh?

98
00:06:09,570 --> 00:06:14,410
By your logic, if I duel you and win,
that proves I'm superior, right?

99
00:06:14,410 --> 00:06:17,790
If that happens, don't you dare
make another move on Ogami!

100
00:06:17,790 --> 00:06:19,710
Noren?

101
00:06:20,750 --> 00:06:22,550
What's this all of a sudden?

102
00:06:22,550 --> 00:06:25,510
But hey, I do prefer things to be simple!

103
00:06:27,010 --> 00:06:30,510
Fine by me! If I win, I get Juzo!

104
00:06:30,510 --> 00:06:33,260
And you never butt in again,
Noren Mitsuoka!

105
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:35,640
It isn't fine by me!

106
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:38,440
How did this turn into a duel over me?

107
00:06:38,810 --> 00:06:41,150
I just said I was sorry, didn't I?

108
00:06:41,150 --> 00:06:43,230
C'mon, it's a duel! No big deal!

109
00:06:43,230 --> 00:06:45,490
It can just be for show at first,

110
00:06:45,490 --> 00:06:47,700
but I'll have you wrapped
around my finger in no time.

111
00:06:48,030 --> 00:06:50,570
Noren! You don't have to duel her, either.

112
00:06:50,570 --> 00:06:53,240
All I have to do is keep turning her down.

113
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:55,500
I promise I won't fall for it,
so it's fine!

114
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:56,950
I know!

115
00:06:56,950 --> 00:06:59,460
I know you probably won't get
any weird ideas.

116
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:02,380
But even if you don't feel that way...

117
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:06,300
watching her do that right in front
of me over and over doesn't sit right.

118
00:07:08,300 --> 00:07:09,550
<i>Uh, Boss?</i>

119
00:07:10,010 --> 00:07:10,800
<i>Is this gonna be...</i>

120
00:07:11,340 --> 00:07:12,260
<i>okay?</i>

121
00:07:12,550 --> 00:07:14,310
All right, it's settled!

122
00:07:14,310 --> 00:07:17,730
Now, the duel lets us choose the contest
and the number of participants,

123
00:07:17,730 --> 00:07:21,440
but I still have to formally challenge
Juzo. That part's the bare minimum.

124
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:25,650
So! It'll be a three-person contest.
Juzo and Mitsuoka versus me.

125
00:07:25,650 --> 00:07:27,360
As for the event, hm...

126
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:28,650
How about surfing?

127
00:07:28,990 --> 00:07:30,320
Bring it on!

128
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:33,530
Whoever rides the best wave wins.

129
00:07:33,530 --> 00:07:35,870
I'll send you the detailed rules later.

130
00:07:35,870 --> 00:07:39,160
See ya, Juzo! Better get ready for me!

131
00:07:39,660 --> 00:07:40,330
Hey!

132
00:07:43,330 --> 00:07:46,090
So, the next opponent is Mai Otohime.

133
00:07:46,090 --> 00:07:49,630
I can't believe they ended up having
a duel after all, and in this form!

134
00:07:49,630 --> 00:07:51,630
Surfing, huh?

135
00:07:51,970 --> 00:07:53,890
Noren, have you ever done it?

136
00:07:54,850 --> 00:07:56,390
Nope. Not once.

137
00:07:56,390 --> 00:07:58,430
Then why did you say, "Bring it on"?

138
00:07:58,430 --> 00:08:01,600
Noren, do you always just charge
straight ahead like this?

139
00:08:02,140 --> 00:08:03,600
What about you, Ogami?

140
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:07,440
This couple's hopeless!
They're gonna get wiped out instantly!

141
00:08:07,900 --> 00:08:09,740
Hey, come to think of it...

142
00:08:10,070 --> 00:08:11,070
Hm?

143
00:08:12,990 --> 00:08:15,410
Second-years and third-years,
gather round!

144
00:08:15,410 --> 00:08:19,450
PSST...
PSST...

145
00:08:20,120 --> 00:08:21,750
Noren... Ogami...

146
00:08:21,750 --> 00:08:23,960
You two are our precious juniors.

147
00:08:23,960 --> 00:08:27,550
And as the home ec club,
we obviously want to support you.

148
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:30,840
But at this rate,
you two don't stand a chance.

149
00:08:30,840 --> 00:08:33,840
You need muscle training!
I mean, special training!

150
00:08:34,220 --> 00:08:35,550
And luckily for us...

151
00:08:35,550 --> 00:08:38,350
next Monday is our school's
founding anniversary.

152
00:08:38,930 --> 00:08:41,890
Add Saturday and Sunday,
and that gives us a three-day weekend.

153
00:08:41,890 --> 00:08:42,850
Which means...

154
00:08:43,810 --> 00:08:45,980
We can do an beach training camp!

155
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:50,030
Yay.

156
00:08:59,660 --> 00:09:03,040
Now I've got more stuff to think about
before training camp.

157
00:09:03,040 --> 00:09:04,750
Coffee, Boss?

158
00:09:05,210 --> 00:09:07,210
I would've brought you some if you'd asked.

159
00:09:07,590 --> 00:09:08,960
It's fine.

160
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:10,590
I just finished my homework,

161
00:09:10,590 --> 00:09:13,260
and I've got stuff on my mind,
so I was gonna come here anyway.

162
00:09:13,670 --> 00:09:17,550
B-B-Boss, haven't you been
way too nice lately?

163
00:09:17,550 --> 00:09:20,010
Hold on. Are you about to die
or something?

164
00:09:20,350 --> 00:09:21,680
Why would I be?

165
00:09:21,680 --> 00:09:24,020
Nothing has been building up to that.

166
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:26,020
I mean...

167
00:09:26,020 --> 00:09:30,020
before you turned back into a kid,
you were a lot harsher.

168
00:09:30,690 --> 00:09:35,400
There was more than one target, you moron!
Do your damn research!

169
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:38,240
And if I got the wrong kind of cigarette,
you'd clock me.

170
00:09:38,490 --> 00:09:41,370
How many times do I gotta tell you
I don't smoke menthols, you idiot?

171
00:09:41,370 --> 00:09:43,750
You were running me
like some live-in yakuza apprentice!

172
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:46,120
You beat every lesson into me!

173
00:09:46,370 --> 00:09:47,880
This coffee's lukewarm!

174
00:09:49,420 --> 00:09:51,130
No, I never...

175
00:09:51,130 --> 00:09:53,130
I totally did. Sorry.

176
00:09:53,130 --> 00:09:55,970
Well, I dunno. Looking back on it, yeah.

177
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:58,220
I didn't realize until you said it...

178
00:09:58,220 --> 00:10:01,930
but maybe the older girls in home ec
have rubbed off on me in a lot of ways.

179
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:06,060
Now you've made this
 awkward to talk about.

180
00:10:06,390 --> 00:10:09,860
The truth is, there's something I need
to ask you about before training camp.

181
00:10:09,860 --> 00:10:11,020
Ask me?

182
00:10:11,020 --> 00:10:15,030
LIFE PATHS
SATURDAY, JUNE 27th

183
00:10:15,030 --> 00:10:17,030
PARENT-TEACHER CONFERENCE

184
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:18,910
A parent-teacher conference?

185
00:10:18,910 --> 00:10:22,280
That thing with the teacher,
student, and parent?

186
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:24,830
Man, just when you've got
that surfing match coming up.

187
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:27,540
What am I gonna do about a parent?

188
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:28,540
DING

189
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:31,790
I got it, boss!
There's a perfect way to handle this!

190
00:10:31,790 --> 00:10:33,210
Huh? Seriously?

191
00:10:33,210 --> 00:10:34,880
Just leave it to me!

192
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:38,380
Oh, right. No club today.

193
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:40,090
Wanna stop somewhere?

194
00:10:40,090 --> 00:10:42,220
Tell me the rest of that story.

195
00:10:42,220 --> 00:10:44,140
Buy me a large fries and nuggets!

196
00:10:44,470 --> 00:10:47,980
- Hey, we're best friends, right?
- Huh? Where's this coming from?

197
00:10:53,610 --> 00:10:55,860
You here for a parent-teacher
conference, too?

198
00:10:55,860 --> 00:10:58,150
No. I'm waiting for Noren.

199
00:10:58,570 --> 00:11:00,490
I feel like, through
that ramen showdown...

200
00:11:00,490 --> 00:11:02,530
we understand each other
on a much deeper level!

201
00:11:02,530 --> 00:11:03,740
No, we absolutely do not!

202
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:07,620
More importantly,
Noren's mother is coming today.

203
00:11:07,620 --> 00:11:09,120
I must offer her my greetings!

204
00:11:09,420 --> 00:11:11,080
Huh? And what are you gonna say?

205
00:11:11,750 --> 00:11:13,210
"It's a pleasure to meet you, Mother."

206
00:11:13,210 --> 00:11:16,090
"I am Shin Kohazame, the man
who will someday have your blessing..."

207
00:11:16,090 --> 00:11:17,590
"to marry Noren."

208
00:11:17,590 --> 00:11:19,380
Yeah, no. You lost the duel.

209
00:11:19,380 --> 00:11:21,510
For now, I'm the fiancÃ©.

210
00:11:21,510 --> 00:11:22,220
What?

211
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:25,390
Then at least let me catch
one tiny glimpse from inside the ceiling!

212
00:11:25,390 --> 00:11:28,060
Stay in there and 
never come out again, you freak!

213
00:11:30,020 --> 00:11:32,520
Oh... You here for a parent-teacher
conference, too?

214
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:34,070
MINE IS ON A DIFFERENT DAY.
I AM WAITING ON MY BROTHER...

215
00:11:34,070 --> 00:11:35,020
I see.

216
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:37,490
Also, you guys sure are close.

217
00:11:38,190 --> 00:11:38,820
Huh?

218
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:40,910
Oga, you're not going home?

219
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:43,200
Nah, today I have a meeting
with my teacher and...

220
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:45,080
Oh, parent-teacher conference?

221
00:11:45,330 --> 00:11:48,080
Wait, Oga's parents
will be coming here soon?

222
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:51,670
Then we gotta say hi!

223
00:11:51,670 --> 00:11:54,500
First impressions are important, y'know!

224
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:56,250
No, you don't! Go home!

225
00:11:57,630 --> 00:11:58,630
Whoa!

226
00:11:58,630 --> 00:11:59,970
Huh? Rindou?

227
00:12:04,970 --> 00:12:08,100
Wait, what?
Oga, are you friends with Rindou?

228
00:12:08,470 --> 00:12:12,560
Huh? Oh, uh, we sort of played
a sport together the other day.

229
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:14,650
Or, well, "golf," I guess!

230
00:12:15,350 --> 00:12:17,400
I DID IT

231
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:21,070
He talks with flip cards? That's adorable!

232
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:22,910
She is really into this.

233
00:12:23,280 --> 00:12:25,490
And wait, his drawings are actually good!

234
00:12:25,490 --> 00:12:28,620
Hey, I like cats! Draw me one!

235
00:12:32,410 --> 00:12:33,960
That got realistic all of a sudden!

236
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:37,130
Not what I expected, but it's still cute!

237
00:12:37,420 --> 00:12:39,460
Okay, I'm actually really happy right now!

238
00:12:40,380 --> 00:12:41,420
Let's go.

239
00:12:43,930 --> 00:12:45,510
What were you talking about?

240
00:12:45,510 --> 00:12:46,390
Meow...

241
00:12:46,390 --> 00:12:47,140
I see.

242
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:51,520
Wait, was that his brother
who just understood "meow"?

243
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:53,520
Yeah. They don't look much alike, though.

244
00:12:54,520 --> 00:12:56,360
He really is so cool!

245
00:12:56,360 --> 00:12:57,980
For real? You think?

246
00:12:58,610 --> 00:13:02,490
That aside, is Nekota gonna be okay?

247
00:13:02,780 --> 00:13:03,610
Oh!

248
00:13:03,610 --> 00:13:05,200
I've got it, Boss!

249
00:13:05,870 --> 00:13:08,240
That face... He thought of something.

250
00:13:08,660 --> 00:13:12,620
He's going to ask someone
to play my parent, isn't he?

251
00:13:12,620 --> 00:13:15,250
He better not have asked Eri!

252
00:13:16,460 --> 00:13:17,750
Juzo!

253
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:19,590
Sorry to keep you waiting!

254
00:13:20,050 --> 00:13:22,210
You showed up in drag?

255
00:13:22,210 --> 00:13:25,130
And why is the outfit just decent enough
to make this awkward?

256
00:13:25,130 --> 00:13:26,470
I don't even know how to react!

257
00:13:26,470 --> 00:13:29,600
If you'd gone all-out terrible,
I could've just smacked you!

258
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:31,470
Is that Oga's mom?

259
00:13:31,470 --> 00:13:33,270
Huh? She doesn't really look like...

260
00:13:33,270 --> 00:13:35,480
I mean, that's pretty different
from what I pictured.

261
00:13:35,810 --> 00:13:38,190
Oh my. Are you Juzo's friends?

262
00:13:38,190 --> 00:13:40,900
Thank you so much
for always looking after him!

263
00:13:40,900 --> 00:13:42,070
Uh, yes.

264
00:13:42,070 --> 00:13:42,940
Nice to meet you.

265
00:13:42,940 --> 00:13:45,320
What kind of mom were you picturing?

266
00:13:45,320 --> 00:13:46,450
Are you stupid, you...

267
00:13:46,450 --> 00:13:48,620
"Stupid"? What kind of child
talks to his mother that way?

268
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:49,910
Is this a rebellious phase? Honestly!

269
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:52,790
Don't worry, Boss!

270
00:13:52,790 --> 00:13:55,710
<i>No matter what happens,
I'll play the perfect mom to the end!</i>

271
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:56,670
I'm a professional!

272
00:13:57,040 --> 00:13:58,540
<i>None of this is getting through to him!</i>

273
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,420
Here you go, girls!

274
00:14:00,790 --> 00:14:02,130
Take some candy!

275
00:14:02,130 --> 00:14:03,590
Catch! Catch!

276
00:14:03,590 --> 00:14:04,630
Uh, thanks.

277
00:14:04,630 --> 00:14:05,550
Thank you.

278
00:14:05,550 --> 00:14:08,140
<i>That's not a mom! That's an Osaka auntie!</i>

279
00:14:09,220 --> 00:14:11,010
Thank you for waiting!

280
00:14:11,010 --> 00:14:12,930
Mrs. Ogami, come on in.

281
00:14:13,430 --> 00:14:14,390
Thank you!

282
00:14:17,190 --> 00:14:19,480
I'm Juzo's mother.

283
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:21,110
Thank you for meeting with us today!

284
00:14:21,650 --> 00:14:24,900
Huh? Oh, yes. Please, have a seat.

285
00:14:24,900 --> 00:14:27,820
She's strangely young,
and they don't look anything alike!

286
00:14:28,410 --> 00:14:32,620
Um, excuse me, but you wouldn't happen
to be Juzo's older sister, would you?

287
00:14:32,620 --> 00:14:35,410
Oh, goodness, Professor!
Aren't you a flatterer!

288
00:14:36,370 --> 00:14:40,750
So, Professor, how is my boy doing?
Is he getting along all right at school?

289
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:43,420
Uh, yes, I would say so.

290
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:45,760
I don't see any problems with his conduct.

291
00:14:45,760 --> 00:14:47,090
He takes class seriously.

292
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:50,550
Juzo, that's a glowing review!

293
00:14:50,550 --> 00:14:52,760
Mommy's so relieved!

294
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:54,770
- Knock it off!
- However...

295
00:14:54,770 --> 00:14:56,640
...there is one issue.

296
00:14:56,640 --> 00:14:57,600
An issue?

297
00:14:57,600 --> 00:14:59,190
Hey! What did you do?

298
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:02,190
Oh, no! I wouldn't call it
a serious issue!

299
00:15:02,190 --> 00:15:05,940
But first, is it okay
to smack him like that?

300
00:15:05,940 --> 00:15:08,150
Oh, my!

301
00:15:08,450 --> 00:15:11,620
One thing that does concern me slightly
is that every now and then...

302
00:15:11,620 --> 00:15:14,490
is the way he talks and acts
is oddly middle-aged, I suppose.

303
00:15:16,450 --> 00:15:18,160
Oh, goodness, really?

304
00:15:18,580 --> 00:15:20,500
I wonder where he gets that from!

305
00:15:20,500 --> 00:15:21,960
- Honestly, this child!
- Ow!

306
00:15:22,790 --> 00:15:24,340
Well, thank you so much!

307
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:27,050
It was a pleasure meeting you!

308
00:15:27,050 --> 00:15:28,220
Likewise.

309
00:15:28,220 --> 00:15:29,630
Thank you for coming in today.

310
00:15:29,630 --> 00:15:30,720
Take care.

311
00:15:30,720 --> 00:15:32,800
When we get home,
I am absolutely kicking his ass.

312
00:15:33,850 --> 00:15:34,470
Huh?

313
00:15:34,890 --> 00:15:35,890
Noren?

314
00:15:35,890 --> 00:15:37,470
Oh, Ogami...

315
00:15:37,770 --> 00:15:40,560
Oh my, Juzo! Another friend?

316
00:15:40,560 --> 00:15:43,480
Goodness, every girl you know is so cute!

317
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:45,070
Cut it out with that act already!

318
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:50,280
This is Ogami's mother? She's completely
different from what I pictured.

319
00:15:50,280 --> 00:15:53,620
Hello there! I'm Juzo Ogami's mother.

320
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:55,830
Thank you for looking after my son!

321
00:15:55,830 --> 00:15:58,790
It's nice to meet you.
I'm Noren Mitsuoka's mother.

322
00:15:58,790 --> 00:16:00,330
Your son takes very good care of her.

323
00:16:00,330 --> 00:16:01,620
Oh! You're from overseas?

324
00:16:01,620 --> 00:16:04,500
You're so beautiful!
And your Japanese is wonderful!

325
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:07,880
Oh, not at all!
I still have so much to learn!

326
00:16:07,880 --> 00:16:10,590
- So, this is Noren's mother.
- No, it really is excellent!

327
00:16:10,590 --> 00:16:12,130
- She's more normal than I expected.
- Where are you from?

328
00:16:12,130 --> 00:16:12,930
Canada.

329
00:16:12,930 --> 00:16:13,930
Oh, my!

330
00:16:13,930 --> 00:16:14,850
Canada?

331
00:16:14,850 --> 00:16:16,430
- The Canada where maple syrup...
- There's no resemblance.

332
00:16:16,430 --> 00:16:17,930
- ...comes out of the faucets?
- Nothing like that!

333
00:16:20,640 --> 00:16:23,230
Well, Boss, we somehow got through that!

334
00:16:23,810 --> 00:16:24,860
So?

335
00:16:24,860 --> 00:16:27,360
How'd I do as your mom?

336
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:29,280
Incredible.

337
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:30,990
So good I want to murder you.

338
00:16:30,990 --> 00:16:32,650
Right?

339
00:16:32,650 --> 00:16:35,280
I actually put a lot of thought
into the makeup.

340
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:38,120
And I really worked out
the character, too!

341
00:16:41,120 --> 00:16:42,620
Nekota, go home without me.

342
00:16:43,120 --> 00:16:43,750
Huh?

343
00:16:44,710 --> 00:16:47,000
I wanna be alone for a bit.

344
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:25,460
He is still only a first-year...

345
00:17:25,460 --> 00:17:29,460
but I'd like to start discussing his future.

346
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:31,710
There's no rush to decide, of course,

347
00:17:31,710 --> 00:17:34,470
but if you're considering high school
 and higher education,

348
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:37,970
it's always best to start preparing early.

349
00:17:38,970 --> 00:17:40,560
My future, huh?

350
00:17:40,890 --> 00:17:43,480
For a middle-aged guy like me,
it should be completely irrelevant,

351
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:46,020
which is probably why it stuck in my head.

352
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:48,610
Master wants to become a doctor.

353
00:17:48,610 --> 00:17:51,230
So, he'll go on to high school,
then college.

354
00:17:51,230 --> 00:17:51,980
Noren...

355
00:17:51,980 --> 00:17:54,110
will probably open a ramen shop someday.

356
00:17:54,110 --> 00:17:57,530
Though I doubt she'd say that
at a parent-teacher conference.

357
00:17:57,530 --> 00:17:58,490
And Tenma said...

358
00:17:58,490 --> 00:18:01,410
he was gonna go pro
in three sports, right?

359
00:18:02,410 --> 00:18:05,250
Knowing him,
he might actually pull it off.

360
00:18:06,210 --> 00:18:08,290
Honestly, school is fun.

361
00:18:08,630 --> 00:18:09,920
But sometimes...

362
00:18:10,250 --> 00:18:13,800
they seem so full of possibility,
I can barely stand to look at them.

363
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:15,260
They've got futures ahead of them,

364
00:18:16,090 --> 00:18:19,760
and I'm an old man who doesn't.

365
00:18:23,180 --> 00:18:25,430
What's all this, Ogami?

366
00:18:26,270 --> 00:18:28,350
You're looking awfully wistful out here.

367
00:18:28,350 --> 00:18:31,440
As usual, you give off
a very non-seventh-grader vibe.

368
00:18:31,820 --> 00:18:33,440
Oh, Big Sis!

369
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:34,900
What are you doing here?

370
00:18:34,900 --> 00:18:37,150
I could ask you.
Why are you here at this hour?

371
00:18:37,530 --> 00:18:40,700
Oh, that's right. Ryo said
you had a parent-teacher conference.

372
00:18:40,700 --> 00:18:42,030
Yeah. Did you have one, too?

373
00:18:42,530 --> 00:18:46,540
Nah, I'm a third-year,
so mine was guidance counseling.

374
00:18:46,540 --> 00:18:49,710
What kind of high school I want to go to, 
how am I handling entrance exams...

375
00:18:49,710 --> 00:18:51,500
That sort of thing.
I have to start deciding.

376
00:18:52,290 --> 00:18:57,170
So, I suppose I came out here
to get lost in thought myself.

377
00:19:04,100 --> 00:19:07,640
So, are you gonna go
to a cooking school or something?

378
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:10,190
Huh? Why would I?

379
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:12,860
I'm planning on going
to a regular academic high school.

380
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:15,150
Huh? That's not what I expected!

381
00:19:15,860 --> 00:19:18,490
You're not going to pursue
the path of cooking?

382
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:21,160
What does "the path of cooking" even mean?

383
00:19:21,700 --> 00:19:23,660
I like cooking, sure...

384
00:19:23,660 --> 00:19:26,160
but that doesn't mean
I want to become a chef.

385
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:29,410
Besides, I don't think you have to
lock in your whole life right now.

386
00:19:30,290 --> 00:19:34,920
Are you thinking everyone's supposed
to have some dream or goal already?

387
00:19:35,300 --> 00:19:39,590
I mean, I do think the way
my little brother and Tenma live is cool.

388
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:42,300
But personally, I'd rather not decide yet.

389
00:19:42,930 --> 00:19:45,140
Once I get to high school,
I'll have more options.

390
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:48,810
Once I get to college,
I'll have even more.

391
00:19:49,180 --> 00:19:51,980
I want to choose how I live
from all of those possibilities.

392
00:19:51,980 --> 00:19:54,980
Isn't that one of the reasons why we study?

393
00:19:54,980 --> 00:19:57,900
Well, I'm not nearly as good at it
as my little brother.

394
00:19:58,860 --> 00:20:00,610
Wait. Could there actually...

395
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:02,610
be one?

396
00:20:02,610 --> 00:20:03,700
Huh?

397
00:20:03,700 --> 00:20:06,990
It's bad for a hitman to come to school?

398
00:20:07,790 --> 00:20:10,910
Back then, it still hadn't clicked.

399
00:20:10,910 --> 00:20:12,420
No matter how this turned out,

400
00:20:12,420 --> 00:20:16,380
I figured once I got my old body back,
I'd just go back to being an assassin.

401
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:19,800
Until now, I've only been studying
because it's fun.

402
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:20,550
GRAMMAR: SUBJECT AND PREDICATE

403
00:20:20,550 --> 00:20:21,680
But...

404
00:20:21,970 --> 00:20:24,550
if I set a goal and 
kept working toward it...

405
00:20:24,550 --> 00:20:25,850
could I have one, too?

406
00:20:50,580 --> 00:20:53,000
A life where I'm not an assassin...

407
00:20:53,710 --> 00:20:54,920
A future...

408
00:20:59,170 --> 00:21:00,130
Huh?

409
00:21:00,460 --> 00:21:02,590
Wait, are you crying, Ogami?

410
00:21:02,590 --> 00:21:03,430
No.

411
00:21:03,430 --> 00:21:05,680
The sunset's just stinging my eyes.

412
00:21:05,680 --> 00:21:06,850
What are you, an old man?

413
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:10,020
No! Huh? As if!

414
00:21:10,470 --> 00:21:13,560
Well! Anyway, my point is, let's enjoy
all kinds of things while we can!

415
00:21:14,230 --> 00:21:16,690
Not just studying, but club stuff, too!

416
00:21:17,310 --> 00:21:20,570
That beach training camp we talked about
is gonna be a blast for everyone!

417
00:21:22,240 --> 00:21:23,070
Huh?

418
00:21:23,570 --> 00:21:25,320
Club President? Ogami?

419
00:21:25,610 --> 00:21:27,070
Oh, Noren!

420
00:21:27,410 --> 00:21:29,950
Are you here for some brooding time, too?

421
00:21:30,240 --> 00:21:31,080
Huh?

422
00:21:31,080 --> 00:21:32,200
Brooding?

423
00:21:32,200 --> 00:21:36,040
Give that duel everything you've got!
That's what the training camp is for.

424
00:21:36,040 --> 00:21:36,920
R-Right!

425
00:21:37,580 --> 00:21:38,630
The ocean...

426
00:21:38,630 --> 00:21:42,460
And we'll have someone coming along
who knows a lot about surfing.

427
00:21:42,460 --> 00:21:43,420
Huh? Who?

428
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:46,640
You'll find out when we get there!

429
00:21:47,470 --> 00:21:49,390
Uh, y-yes, ma'am.

430
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:55,770
When am I gonna turn back to normal?

431
00:21:55,770 --> 00:21:58,230
Or am I stuck like this forever?

432
00:21:58,230 --> 00:22:01,230
Well, there's no point sitting around
thinking about it.

433
00:22:01,230 --> 00:22:02,650
What happens, happens.

434
00:22:03,280 --> 00:22:05,030
Hell, this could be interesting.

435
00:22:05,030 --> 00:22:07,200
I'm used to trouble!

436
00:22:07,200 --> 00:22:10,030
And I'll blast right through
every last bit of it!

437
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:45,000
KILL BLUE SEASON 2 CONFIRMED!!

